[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Play Cyberpunk 2077 in [b]real stereoscopic 3D[/b], side by side for any [b]3D display / VR headset with SBS support[/b], on a big virtual screen with real depth.

[b]Not VR: no head tracking, no motion controls![/b] You look at a 3D screen.

Patch 2.5 added a 3D Mode for a glasses-free 3D monitor, with real depth for the world, the HUD and your weapon, but only when that monitor's software is installed. This mod:
[list=1]
[*]Provides a small stand-in for that software, so [b]3D Mode[/b] unlocks on a normal monitor.[/*]
[*]Turns on a hidden engine option so the game draws the eyes [b]side by side[/b].[/*]
[*]Makes [b]menus readable[/b]: menus, the map and loading screens are squeezed into each eye.[/*]
[/list]
[b]It's the game's own stereo renderer, not a depth-map effect.[/b]

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url].[/*]
[*]Install this mod with Vortex (or extract it into the game folder with [i]bin[/i], [i]engine[/i] and [i]red4ext[/i]).[/*]
[*]In the game's video settings, turn on [b]3D Mode[/b] (this turns the game's Frame Generation off). You now see two images side by side.[/*]
[*]In your headset, show the PC screen in [b]half side-by-side[/b] 3D (in Virtual Desktop: the desktop screen's 3D mode). The game must run on the monitor the headset shows.[/*]
[/list]
To play in 2D, turn 3D Mode off in the game Video settings.
[b]Uninstall:[/b] remove the mod in Vortex ([url=https://github.com/vl3c/cyberpunk2077-3d-braindance-edition#no-red4ext-uninstall-and-other-details]details[/url]).

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Depth tuned with the game's own settings: [b]Preset[/b], [b]Depth[/b], [b]Weapon Depth[/b] and [b]Motion Comfort[/b]. Depth 0.5 to 1.0 works well in a headset.[/*]
[*][b]No game files modified.[/b] The game loads the stand-in DLL through its own 3D support; only the menu fix uses a small RED4ext hook.[/*]
[*]Sets itself up at every game start.[/*]
[/list]
[b]Good to know:[/b]
[list]
[*]Each eye gets half the horizontal resolution, so [b]higher resolution looks sharper[/b]. Every frame renders twice, so expect a lower frame rate than in 2D. I recommend a [b]4K (virtual) monitor in Virtual Desktop[/b] and OptiScaler frame generation: see the [url=https://github.com/vl3c/cyberpunk2077-3d-braindance-edition#recommended-setup-quest-3--virtual-desktop]recommended setup[/url].[/*]
[*]Stereo 3D can strain your eyes: take breaks and lower Depth if needed.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 [b]2.5[/b] on Windows 10 or 11. Tested on Epic; Steam and GOG untested.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/2380]RED4ext[/url]. Without it, use the setup script from the [url=https://github.com/vl3c/cyberpunk2077-3d-braindance-edition#no-red4ext]GitHub download[/url] (menus then stay split).[/*]
[*]A 3D / VR headset with [b]half-SBS support[/b], or a 3D TV or monitor with an SBS mode. Tested: Quest 3 with [url=https://www.vrdesktop.net/]Virtual Desktop[/url].[/*]
[*]Own a glasses-free 3D monitor the game supports? Don't install this mod: it switches the game to side-by-side output.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Shout outs[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]CD PROJEKT RED[/b], for building a full stereo 3D renderer into Cyberpunk 2077.[/*]
[*][b]Guy Godin[/b], for Virtual Desktop and its SBS mode.[/*]
[*][b]Claude[/b] (Anthropic's AI), my co-pilot on this one: reverse engineering the game's 3D interface, writing the stand-in and the RED4ext plugin, and testing it with me.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]
Settings and logs are in [i]bin\x64\Braindance3D[/i] (logs go to [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Braindance3D[/i] if the game folder is read-only).
[list]
[*][b]Crash or no start after installing or a game update:[/b] disable the mod and report your game version.[/*]
[*][b]3D Mode greyed out:[/b] check RED4ext and read [i]Braindance3D-autosetup.log[/i]. With several monitors, set [i]Monitor = primary[/i] in [i]Braindance3D-Settings.ini[/i] and play on it.[/*]
[*][b]Menus look wrong:[/b] set [i]Squeeze = off[/i] under [i][Menus][/i] and report with [i]Braindance3D-hooks.log[/i].[/*]
[*][b]Depth inside out:[/b] use your viewer's swap-eyes option.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]OptiScaler's own menu and FPS counter still look split ([i]FpsOverlayPos = 0[/i] keeps the counter readable in the left eye).[/*]
[*]Mod Organizer 2 isn't supported yet.[/*]
[*]Untested: multi-monitor setups, viewers other than Virtual Desktop.[/*]
[/list]
[size=4][b]Bugs[/b][/size]
Use the Bugs tab or [url=https://github.com/vl3c/cyberpunk2077-3d-braindance-edition/issues]GitHub issues[/url]. Include game version and store, GPU, how you view the 3D, and the logs ([i]braindance3d.log[/i], [i]Braindance3D-autosetup.log[/i], [i]Braindance3D-hooks.log[/i]) with [i]Level = 2[/i] in the settings file. Logs contain folder paths, which can include your Windows user name.

